{"id":"st2067-50","designation":"ST 2067-50","title":"Interoperable Master Format (IMF) — Application #5 ACES","state":"active","suite":"2067","official":{"family_url":"https://pub.smpte.org/doc/st2067-50/","latest_url":"https://pub.smpte.org/latest/st2067-50/","checked_at":"2026-11-18"},"scope":"This document specifies Compositions for IMF Application #5. It is a specialization of the IMF Framework. Application #5 targets archival applications where a TV or movie title is to be archived as a single, high-quality set of master files from which one or more content versions can be derived. It features SMPTE ST 2065-1 (ACES) image essence of arbitrary spatial and temporal resolution with individual frames encoded as ACES images. The transformation of Application #5 Compositions to the output formats appropriate for different distribution channels is specified in other documents and outside the scope of this document. To facilitate Output Profile List processing, Annex A defines Pixel Color Schemes , as specified in SMPTE ST 2067-101, for the use with IMF Application #5.","outline":[{"level":1,"title":"1 Scope","page":4},{"level":1,"title":"2 Conformance Notation","page":4},{"level":1,"title":"3 Normative References","page":5},{"level":1,"title":"4 Terms and Definitions","page":6},{"level":2,"title":"4.1 ACES image","page":6},{"level":2,"title":"4.2 Target Frame","page":6},{"level":1,"title":"5 Overall","page":6},{"level":2,"title":"5.1 General","page":6},{"level":2,"title":"5.2 Format","page":6},{"level":2,"title":"5.3 Shim Parameters","page":6},{"level":1,"title":"6 Image Essence","page":7},{"level":2,"title":"6.1 General","page":7},{"level":2,"title":"6.2 Constraints (Informative)","page":7},{"level":2,"title":"6.3 Characteristics","page":7},{"level":3,"title":"6.3.1 Frame Dimensions (Informative)","page":7},{"level":3,"title":"6.3.2 Frame Structure (Informative)","page":8},{"level":3,"title":"6.3.3 Frame Rate","page":8},{"level":3,"title":"6.3.4 Color Components (In